sequenceDiagram
    participant SP as Startup Process
    participant SM as Shared Memory
    participant CP as Checkpointer
    participant BUF as Buffer Pool
    participant DISK as Storage

    Note over SP,DISK: Checkpointer Coordination During WAL Replay

    %% Normal Operation Cycle
    SP->>SP: PerformWalRecovery()
    Note right of SP: Continuous WAL replay

    SP->>+BUF: Buffer allocation for replay
    BUF->>BUF: Check buffer availability
    BUF-->>-SP: Buffers allocated

    %% Memory Pressure Detection
    BUF->>BUF: Monitor buffer pool usage
    Note right of BUF: Track dirty buffer count

    alt Memory Pressure Detected
        BUF->>+SM: Signal memory pressure
        Note right of SM: High dirty buffer ratio

        SM->>+CP: SetLatch(&checkpointerLatch)
        Note right of CP: Wake checkpointer process

        CP->>CP: CheckpointerMain() loop
        CP->>CP: Detect checkpoint request

        CP->>+SM: RequestCheckpoint processing
        Note right of SM: Atomic flag setting

        SM->>SM: SpinLockAcquire(&ckpt_lck)
        SM->>SM: Set ckpt_flags |= CHECKPOINT_FORCE
        SM->>SM: SpinLockRelease(&ckpt_lck)
        SM-->>-CP: Request acknowledged

        %% Checkpoint vs Restartpoint Decision
        CP->>CP: Check RecoveryInProgress()
        Note right of CP: Determine checkpoint type

        alt Recovery In Progress
            CP->>CP: CreateRestartPoint()
            Note right CP: Recovery-specific checkpoint
        else Normal Operation
            CP->>CP: CreateCheckPoint()
            Note right of CP: Full checkpoint
        end

        %% Buffer Synchronization Phase
        CP->>+BUF: BufferSync(flags)
        Note right of BUF: Coordinate with ongoing replay

        BUF->>BUF: Mark buffers with BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED
        Note right of BUF: Two-phase buffer processing

        loop For Each Dirty Buffer
            BUF->>BUF: Check BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED flag

            alt Buffer Needs Checkpoint
                BUF->>+DISK: SyncOneBuffer()
                Note right of DISK: Write dirty buffer

                DISK->>DISK: Write buffer page
                DISK-->>-BUF: Write complete

                BUF->>BUF: Clear BM_CHECKPOINT_NEEDED

                %% Coordination with Replay
                BUF->>SP: CheckpointWriteDelay()
                Note left of SP: Throttle I/O for replay progress

                SP->>SP: HandleStartupProcInterrupts()
                Note right of SP: Process signals during delay

                SP-->>BUF: Continue checkpoint
            end
        end

        BUF-->>-CP: BufferSync complete

        %% Completion Notification
        CP->>+SM: Update checkpoint completion
        SM->>SM: SpinLockAcquire(&ckpt_lck)
        SM->>SM: ckpt_done = ckpt_started
        SM->>SM: SpinLockRelease(&ckpt_lck)
        SM->>SM: ConditionVariableBroadcast(&done_cv)
        SM-->>-CP: Completion signaled

        CP-->>-SM: Checkpoint complete
        SM-->>-BUF: Memory pressure relieved
    end

    %% Continuous Coordination Loop
    loop During Active Replay
        SP->>SP: Apply WAL record
        SP->>BUF: Read/modify buffer pages

        %% Buffer State Management
        BUF->>BUF: Mark buffer dirty
        Note right of BUF: Set BM_DIRTY flag

        %% Background Cleaning Coordination
        alt Background Cleaning Triggered
            CP->>+BUF: Background buffer cleaning
            Note right of BUF: Clean buffers without checkpoint

            BUF->>BUF: Select clean candidates
            Note right of BUF: LRU-based selection

            BUF->>+DISK: Write clean buffers
            DISK-->>-BUF: Cleaning complete

            BUF-->>-CP: Background cleaning done
        end

        %% Timeline Switch Coordination
        alt Timeline Switch Detected
            SP->>SP: Process timeline change
            Note right of SP: readTimeLineHistory()

            SP->>+CP: RequestCheckpoint(CHECKPOINT_FORCE)
            Note right of CP: Ensure consistency before switch

            CP->>CP: Force immediate checkpoint
            CP-->>-SP: Checkpoint complete

            SP->>SP: Continue with new timeline
        end

        %% Recovery Target Coordination
        alt Recovery Target Reached
            SP->>SP: Prepare for promotion
            Note right of SP: End of recovery processing

            SP->>+CP: RequestCheckpoint(CHECKPOINT_END_OF_RECOVERY)
            Note right of CP: Special end-recovery checkpoint

            CP->>CP: CreateCheckPoint() [not restartpoint]
            Note right of CP: Real checkpoint during recovery

            CP-->>-SP: End-recovery checkpoint complete

            SP->>SP: Complete recovery process
        end
    end

    %% Error Handling Coordination
    alt Checkpointer Error
        CP->>CP: Checkpoint failure detected
        Note right of CP: I/O error or resource exhaustion

        CP->>+SM: Mark checkpoint failed
        SM->>SM: ckpt_failed++
        SM->>SM: ConditionVariableBroadcast(&done_cv)
        SM-->>-CP: Failure recorded

        CP->>CP: Schedule retry with backoff
        Note right of CP: 15-second retry delay

        alt Startup Process Waiting
            SP->>SP: Check checkpoint completion
            SP->>SM: Wait on condition variable
            SM->>SP: Timeout or failure notification
            SP->>SP: Continue without checkpoint
            Note right of SP: Degrade gracefully
        end
    end

    %% Performance Optimization
    Note over SP,DISK: Performance Coordination Strategies

    %% I/O Bandwidth Management
    CP->>CP: Monitor I/O bandwidth usage
    Note right of CP: Balance checkpoint vs replay I/O

    alt High Replay I/O Rate
        CP->>CP: Reduce checkpoint aggressiveness
        Note right of CP: Increase completion_target

        CP->>BUF: Larger write batches
        Note right of BUF: Reduce I/O overhead

        CP->>SP: Brief yield periods
        Note left of SP: Allow replay progress
    end

    %% Adaptive Checkpoint Timing
    CP->>CP: Calculate optimal checkpoint interval
    Note right of CP: Based on WAL generation rate

    CP->>SM: Update checkpoint scheduling
    Note right of SM: Adaptive timing logic

    %% Resource Contention Minimization
    Note over BUF: Buffer Lock Coordination
    BUF->>BUF: Minimize lock hold times
    Note right of BUF: Quick spinlock operations

    BUF->>SP: Coordinated buffer access
    Note left of SP: Avoid lock contention

    Note over SP,DISK: End Checkpointer Coordination